	// mix(a, b, 1) is b \u2014 so outside a transition the "current" map's taps are
	// dead weight on every density sample. The blend is a uniform, so this
	// branch is coherent across the whole pass; a driver cannot fold it away
	// on its own. (At the endpoints the result differs from the mix by at most
	// one ulp, and only if the implementation lowers mix to an fma.)
